Sitting in a safari car, I don't have to search too far
To feel your presence and your footsteps.
My hat is big, and hair blowing back in the wind,
And something tells me you will smell us from afar.
 
Little hair on your big head, running toward me—
I think I am dead,  
But I feel your love instead.

I am so grateful that you choose to be kind.
When you can crush me, you cuddle up and ask for snacks this time.
You are a gentle, gentle baby giant—
Like I will, and you will too, forever keep each other in mind.

I am humbled by your kind, standing tall and strong right behind.
Grey skins and intelligent minds, ivory tusks and expressive eyes,
The ever-listening ears and strong trumpets—
Your strength is unmatched, you have my respect.
 
